@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Teacher Creates an Assignment

actor Teacher
participant "Vue.js SPA\n(in Browser)" as FrontendApp
participant "NGINX Ingress Controller" as Ingress
participant "Assignment Service Pod" as AssignmentServicePod
participant "Authentication Service Pod" as AuthServicePod
database "MongoDB\n(Assignments DB)" as DBAssignment

Teacher -> FrontendApp: Fills & submits new assignment form\n(title, students list, etc.)
activate FrontendApp

FrontendApp -> Ingress: **POST /assignments** (HTTPS)\n{body: assignmentData, header: Auth: Bearer **jwt**}
activate Ingress

note right of Ingress
  **Path-Based Routing:**
  Path "/assignments" matches the rule
  for the Assignment Service.
end note
Ingress -> AssignmentServicePod: **POST /assignments** (HTTP)\n{body: assignmentData, header: Auth: Bearer **jwt**}
note right of Ingress: Path is preserved (no rewrite)
activate AssignmentServicePod

' Step 1: JWT Validation and Role Check (local)
AssignmentServicePod -> AssignmentServicePod: Decode token & check claims (role, expiration)
alt#LightCoral #White Invalid Token or Role != 'teacher'
    AssignmentServicePod --> Ingress: HTTP 401/403\n{"error": "Unauthorized"}\n
    Ingress --> FrontendApp: HTTP 401/403 Response
    deactivate AssignmentServicePod
    deactivate Ingress
    FrontendApp -> Teacher: Show Error Message
    deactivate FrontendApp
end

' Step 2 (Optional): Enrich teacher data by calling Auth Service
' This step might not be necessary if the JWT already contains all needed info.
' For this diagram, we assume it's done for completeness.
note right of AssignmentServicePod
  Calls Auth service to get teacher's
  full details if needed.
end note
AssignmentServicePod -> Ingress: **GET /auth/users/me** (HTTP) \nHeader: Auth: Bearer **jwt**
activate Ingress
Ingress -> AuthServicePod: **GET /auth/users/me** (HTTP) \nHeader: Auth: Bearer **jwt**
activate AuthServicePod
AuthServicePod --> Ingress: HTTP 200 OK {user_details}
deactivate AuthServicePod
Ingress --> AssignmentServicePod: HTTP 200 OK {user_details}
deactivate Ingress

' Step 3: Validate student list by calling Auth Service
note right of AssignmentServicePod
  Calls Auth service to validate the
  list of student serial numbers.
end note
AssignmentServicePod -> Ingress: **POST /auth/users/validate** (HTTP)\n{serials: [...]}, Header: Auth: Bearer **jwt**
activate Ingress
Ingress -> AuthServicePod: **POST /auth/users/validate** (HTTP)\n{serials: [...]}, Header: Auth: Bearer **jwt**
activate AuthServicePod
AuthServicePod --> Ingress: HTTP 200 {valid: true} / HTTP 400 {error}
deactivate AuthServicePod
Ingress --> AssignmentServicePod: HTTP 200 {valid: true} / HTTP 400 {error}
deactivate Ingress

alt#LightCoral #White Student validation fails
    AssignmentServicePod --> Ingress: HTTP 400\n{"error": "One or more students not found"}
    Ingress --> FrontendApp: HTTP 400 Response
    deactivate AssignmentServicePod
    FrontendApp -> Teacher: Show Error Message
    deactivate FrontendApp
end

' Step 4: Create and save the assignment in its own database
AssignmentServicePod -> AssignmentServicePod: build_assignment_object(...)
AssignmentServicePod -> DBAssignment: insert_one(assignment_object)
activate DBAssignment
DBAssignment --> AssignmentServicePod: {mongo_object_id}
deactivate DBAssignment

AssignmentServicePod -> AssignmentServicePod: Prepare final response object
AssignmentServicePod --> Ingress: **HTTP 201 Created**\n{assignment_object_with_id}
deactivate AssignmentServicePod

Ingress --> FrontendApp: **HTTPS 201 Created**\n{assignment_object_with_id}
deactivate Ingress

FrontendApp -> Teacher: Display "Assignment Created" confirmation
deactivate FrontendApp

@enduml